# Vercel releases

Apply these defaults when the user asks to push, ship, deploy, or optimise deployments. Ordinary editing is not permission to release; respect "commit only" or "do not deploy".

- Production branch: `main`
- Git remote: `origin` (`git@github.com:alex-severino/artbritannia.git`)
- Vercel project: `artbritannia` (team `realbenficas-projects`)
- Serving domain: `https://www.artbritannia.com` (also `artbritannia.com`)
- Fast release: `npm run ship` (push + cached direct deploy). Deploy without push: `npm run deploy`. Read-only check: `npm run deploy -- --check`. Safeguard tests: `npm run test:deploy`.
- Require a clean working tree on `main`. Push the exact commit before deploying local project files. Cancel only pending Git-triggered production builds for that exact commit on `main`. Preserve preview builds, other commits, and CLI deployments.
- Skip rebuilding only when the serving deployment is READY and carries `artbritanniaVerifiedCommit` for that SHA.
- Keep automatic Git deployments enabled. Prefer `npm run ship` to avoid duplicate jobs and the slower Git clone path.
- Preserve original media bytes, dimensions, and quality. Keep media in Git. Do not add storage services or force-push without explicit approval.
- After releasing, verify the remote commit and that the live deployment is READY before reporting success.
